fields.value:
{{Debuffnotes
| name = Savage Roar
| desc = The {{M|fear}} component does not affect [[debuff immune]] enemy units. Other ability effects still apply.
}}
{{Stealnotes
| name = Savage Roar
| desc = The simultaneous Savage Roar cast by either units are not considered as the last cast ability.<br><br>The {{H|Spirit Bear}} summoned does not have this ability unless it is acquired as well.
}}

 * This ability has two main components:
** [[File:Dota2 Condition-1.png|1|21px]]
*** The ability is cast by Lone Druid and the {{H|Spirit Bear}} simultaneously, no matter who was given the order.
*** If either units cannot cast the ability while affected by {{M|disable}} sources, the ability will not be cast.
**** {{cf|shdnotes}} The {{M|Aghanim's Shard|text=ability upgrade}} removes this restriction, and ignores the current {{M|cooldown|text=downtime}} status of either units.
***** Hence, it does not prevent the ability cast if it is still on cooldown on either units.
** [[File:Dota2 Condition-2.png|2|21px]]
*** The ability effects are applied as follows:
***# {{Symbol|Affect|Enemy}}
***#* Applies {{Symbol|Modifier|Debuff}} {{Code|lone_druid_savage_roar}} to all affected enemy units:
***#** {{M|Cannot act}}
***#** {{M|Disarm}}
***#** {{M|Fountain-fear}}
***#** {{M|Muted}}
***#** {{M|Silence}}
***#** Offensively grants bonus {{M|movement speed}}.
***#* Affects the following units:
***#** {{M|Fogged}} units.
***#** {{M|Invisible}} units.
***#** Enemy {{M|Summons|text=player-controlled units}}.
***#* Does not affect the following units:
***#** {{M|Hidden}} units.
***#** {{M|Invulnerable}} units.
***# {{cf|shdnotes}} {{Symbol|Modifier|Buff}} {{Code|lone_druid_rabid}}
***#* {{Symbol|Affect|Self}}
***#** Applies the {{M|basic dispel}} on both Lone Druid and the {{H|Spirit Bear}}.
***#* {{Symbol|Affect|Ally}}
***#** Grants bonus {{M|movement speed}} and bonus {{M|attack speed}} to all allied units within the radius upon cast.

 {{Gamedesc
| image = {{#var:Savage Roar icon0}}
| desc = Lone Druid and the Spirit Bear roar fiercely causing nearby enemies to flee towards their base in terror. Their movement speed is increased by 20%.
}}
* The {{H|Spirit Bear}}'s {{A|Spirit Bear|Savage Roar}} has a 0.64-{{M|cast backswing}}.

